Aim

To create a custom Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) with public and private subnets, configure routing and security, launch EC2 instances, and test secure connectivity within the VPC environment.

Procedure
Step 1: Create the VPC
Login to Amazon Web Services AWS Management Console.
Go to:
Services → VPC
Click Create VPC.
Select:
VPC only
Enter:
Name: Custom-VPC

IPv4 CIDR Block:

10.0.0.0/16
Click Create VPC.
Step 2: Create Public and Private Subnets
Create Public Subnet
Go to:
Subnets → Create Subnet
Select created VPC.
Configure:
Subnet Name: Public-Subnet
Availability Zone: AZ-A

CIDR Block:

10.0.1.0/24
Click Create Subnet.
Create Private Subnet
Again click Create Subnet.
Configure:
Subnet Name: Private-Subnet
Availability Zone: AZ-A

CIDR Block:

10.0.2.0/24
Click Create Subnet.
Step 3: Create and Attach Internet Gateway
Go to:
Internet Gateways
Click Create Internet Gateway.

Enter Name:

Custom-IGW
Click Create Internet Gateway.
Select created IGW.
Click:
Actions → Attach to VPC
Select Custom-VPC.
Click Attach.
Step 4: Create Route Tables
Create Public Route Table
Go to:
Route Tables → Create Route Table
Configure:
Name: Public-RT
Select Custom-VPC
Click Create Route Table.
Add Internet Route
Open Public-RT.
Go to:
Routes → Edit Routes
Add route:
Destination	Target
0.0.0.0/0	Internet Gateway
Save changes.
Associate Public Subnet
Go to:
Subnet Associations
Click Edit Subnet Associations.
Select Public-Subnet.
Save.
Create Private Route Table
Create another route table:
Name: Private-RT
Associate it with:
Private-Subnet
Keep only default local route.
Step 5: Enable Auto-Assign Public IP
Open:
Subnets
Select Public-Subnet.
Click:
Actions → Edit Subnet Settings
Enable:
Auto-assign Public IPv4 Address
Save changes.
Step 6: Configure Security Groups
Go to:
Security Groups → Create Security Group
Configure:
Name: Web-SG
Select Custom-VPC
Add Inbound Rules
Type	Port	Source
SSH	22	My IP
HTTP	80	Anywhere
HTTPS	443	Anywhere
Save security group.
Step 7: Launch EC2 Instances
Launch Public EC2
Go to EC2 → Launch Instance.
Configure:
Select Amazon Linux/Ubuntu AMI
Choose t2.micro
Select Public-Subnet
Enable Public IP
Attach Web-SG.
Launch instance.
Launch Private EC2
Launch another EC2 instance.
Select:
Private-Subnet
Disable Public IP.
Attach appropriate security group.
Launch instance.
Step 8: Test the Setup
Test Public EC2
SSH into Public EC2:
ssh -i key.pem ec2-user@public-ip
Verify internet access:
ping google.com
Test Private EC2
Verify:
No direct internet access
No direct inbound SSH from internet
If NAT Gateway exists, test outbound internet connectivity.
Observation
Custom VPC created successfully.
Public and private subnets configured.
Internet Gateway attached to VPC.
Route tables associated correctly.
Public EC2 accessed internet successfully.
Private EC2 remained isolated from direct internet access.
Result

Successfully created a custom VPC with public and private subnets, configured routing and security, launched EC2 instances, and verified secure connectivity within the AWS VPC environment.
